Manual review corrections, all local typographic defects rather than
upstream OpenStax content issues:

- The resistors exercise trapped the closing parenthesis of "(measured in
  ohms, ..., $\Omega)$" inside math mode; moved it outside to
  "$\Omega$)". The same exercise also wrapped the second resistor's rate
  in a doubly-nested `$1.1\text{$\Omega$/min}$` construct instead of
  matching the first resistor's own `$0.5\,\Omega/\text{min}$` form;
  rewrote it to match.
- The 25-ft-ladder exercise used the built-in LaTeX trig operator `\sec`
  to abbreviate "5 sec", rendering it as a secant invocation rather than
  a time unit. Replaced with `$5\,\text{sec}$`, matching this file's own
  `$20\,\text{ft}$` convention two words earlier in the same sentence.
- Two exercises (bikes to a restaurant; parallel freeways) trapped a
  sentence comma inside the math span itself
  (`$4\,\text{mi,}$`, `$55\,\text{mph,}$`). Moved each comma outside the
  math span.
- The lamppost-shadow figure description left the variable expressions
  "10 + x" and "x" as bare prose instead of math. Wrapped them as
  `$10 + x$` and `$x$`.

